[h2]Commanders![/h2]

We're deeply grateful for the support you've shown us since the release of our game. It brings us immense joy to see so many of you diving into the world of Zoria and embarking on this adventure we put so much work in. Your feedback has been invaluable to us. Each comment, suggestion, and critique is a stepping stone that helps us improve and grow. We truly appreciate your active participation in making Zoria the best it can be.

[h3]We kindly encourage you to continue sharing your thoughts and experiences through reviews.[/h3]
As a small development team, these reviews are more than just ratings for us. They provide us with insights into what works, what doesn't, and what could be improved. They help us understand your perspective better and enable us to make necessary adjustments to enhance your overall experience.

With that said, let's get to the Patch Notes and things we fixed!

[h2]Patch 1.0.1[/h2]
⚔️We are aware that some players encounter a soft-lock combat bug at the end of the combat. We have tested intensively the fix in patch 1.0.1 and believe that the issue is resolved. We will keep testing for any potential issues, please let us know if you encounter this issue again.
⚔️ Using Wizard Ice Wall ability during combat no longer causes a soft-lock in case of a character dying near it;
⚔️ Ability buffs are properly removed from the UI after the end of a combat;
⚔️ Enemies in “Chamber of the Forgotten” now match player’s level;
⚔️ You no longer have to be left forgotten in “Chamber of the Forgotten”. You will be able to exit location after completing the quest;
⚔️ Lancer class resting bonus (gear repair) no longer requires items to be broken;
⚔️ Fixed problems with various quest not completing or disappearing from the quest log as expected;
⚔️ You can now complete the “Lost recipe” quest;
⚔️ Fixed some localization issues;
⚔️ Slightly increased distance between followers in formation;
⚔️ Fixed issue with binding of E/Q keyboard keys. We work on improving support for more key customization feature for future patches.

[h3]What's next?[/h3]
We're already working on a bigger patch which will address the quality of life improvements based on the community feedback and reviews. 

If you happen to come across any bugs, please let us know about it by using this form [[url=https://forms.gle/nB5t2MnB7yHFp1S4A][b]link[/b][/url]]. By filling out the form, we will learn firsthand about any potential issues and it will be much easier for us to track and solve them. Thank you!

See you in the next update,
Tiny Trinket Games

Follow us on [url=https://twitter.com/ZoriaGame][b]Twitter[/b][/url] and join our [url=https://discord.com/invite/k3fPxX8][b]Discord[/b][/url] if you haven't already 😉
